From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:02:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PVE backup: vma reader: reject invalid block info instead of
 aborting

An extent header naming a device that the archive does not have, or a
cluster past the end of the device, triggered an assertion in the
bitmap lookup on verify, and for the cluster also on restore, instead
of an error. The same happened for the last cluster of a device whose
size is not a multiple of 512 bytes, as the bitmap was sized by whole
sectors.

The archive writer never produces any of these and the header checksum
catches random corruption, so only a crafted or broken archive could
trigger it. Still, check the device and cluster before the lookup and
size the bitmap by clusters, so such archives get rejected with an
error like any other malformed one.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Acked-by: Wolfgang Bumiller <w.bumiller@proxmox.com>
---
 vma-reader.c | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vma-reader.c b/vma-reader.c
index d31107a8ca..8350fe89cb 100644
--- a/vma-reader.c
+++ b/vma-reader.c
@@ -455,9 +455,8 @@ static void allocate_rstate(VmaReader *vmar,  guint8 dev_id,
 
     int64_t size = vmar->devinfo[dev_id].size;
 
-    int64_t bitmap_size = (size/BDRV_SECTOR_SIZE) +
-        (VMA_CLUSTER_SIZE/BDRV_SECTOR_SIZE) * BITS_PER_LONG - 1;
-    bitmap_size /= (VMA_CLUSTER_SIZE/BDRV_SECTOR_SIZE) * BITS_PER_LONG;
+    int64_t bitmap_size = DIV_ROUND_UP(DIV_ROUND_UP(size, VMA_CLUSTER_SIZE),
+                                       BITS_PER_LONG);
 
     vmar->rstate[dev_id].bitmap_size = bitmap_size;
     vmar->rstate[dev_id].bitmap = g_new0(unsigned long, bitmap_size);
@@ -642,11 +641,17 @@ static int restore_extent(VmaReader *vmar, unsigned char *buf,
 
         if (dev_id != vmar->vmstate_stream) {
             target = rstate->target;
-            if (!verify && !target && !skip) {
+            if (!rstate->bitmap || (!verify && !target && !skip)) {
                 error_setg(errp, "got wrong dev id %d", dev_id);
                 return -1;
             }
 
+            if (cluster_num >= DIV_ROUND_UP(vmar->devinfo[dev_id].size,
+                                            VMA_CLUSTER_SIZE)) {
+                error_setg(errp, "got wrong block address - write beyond end");
+                return -1;
+            }
+
             if (!skip) {
                 if (vma_reader_get_bitmap(rstate, cluster_num)) {
                     error_setg(errp, "found duplicated cluster %zd for stream %s",
